{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1197854-demons-operating-in-modern-beijing","id":1197854,"title":"Demons Operating in Modern Beijing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-20T20:08:11-07:00","id":1197854,"title":"Demons Operating in Modern Beijing","content":"Some background:<br /> <a href=\"https://qz.com/1232988/after-faces-china-is-moving-quickly-to-identify-people-by-their-voices/\" target=\"_blank\">https://qz.com/1232988/after-faces-c...-their-voices/</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.theatlantic.com/international/archive/2018/02/china-surveillance/552203/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.theatlantic.com/internat...llance/552203/</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/2018/04/big-in-china-machines-that-scan-your-face/554075/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine...r-face/554075/</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2018/3/12/17110636/china-police-facial-recognition-sunglasses-surveillance\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/chorus/uploads/chorus_asset/file/10409609/915205050.jpg.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C11.427293018854%2C100%2C77.145413962291&amp;w=1200\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2018/3/12/17110636/china-police-facial-recognition-sunglasses-surveillance\" target=\"_blank\"> Chinese police are expanding facial recognition sunglasses program </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2018/3/12/17110636/china-police-facial-recognition-sunglasses-surveillance\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.theverge.com/2018/3/12/17110636/china-police-facial-recognition-sunglasses-surveillance </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Police are using the sunglasses to check travelers. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2018/3/16/17130366/china-social-credit-travel-plane-train-tickets\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/chorus/uploads/chorus_asset/file/10440451/632557332.jpg.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C10.916597593092%2C100%2C78.166804813816&amp;w=1200\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2018/3/16/17130366/china-social-credit-travel-plane-train-tickets\" target=\"_blank\"> China will ban people with poor &lsquo;social credit&rsquo; from planes and trains </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2018/3/16/17130366/china-social-credit-travel-plane-train-tickets\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.theverge.com/2018/3/16/17130366/china-social-credit-travel-plane-train-tickets </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The new restrictions, which start in May, can last for up to a year </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It strikes me that this is an interesting environment for an Unchained to operate it. &quot;Social Credit&quot; becomes something that can be pacted to a suitably desperate individuals, and embeds like Vox or Lost in the Crowd can make a demon effectively invisible to surveillance... <i>unless</i> the Chinese government/ intelligence community has an equivalent of Task Force Valkyrie, angelic agents placed in key positions, or if the Deva Corporation is one of the corporations handling the data analytics.<br /> <br /> So... any thoughts?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T21:26:55-07:00","id":1197886,"title":"","content":"This is kind of a personal bugbear for me: I would think critically about whether US media that isn't drawing on Chinese-language sources and reporting and is primed to view China as an enemy nation is going to be a totally reliable source about how the social credit system works in reality. Here's an additional point of view on it: <a href=\"https://twitter.com/isgoodrum/status/975536363364696064\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/isgoodrum/status/975536363364696064</a><br /> <br /> Having said that, yeah, impersonal data collection systems like this (or indeed your credit score in the US) are great for pacts and very on-brand for Demon and the God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64